From: Z User <z@container>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 23:46:20 +0000
Subject: [STAGE 2/3] Stage 3: Super Admin backend + subscription/billing
 foundation
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds Super Admin management APIs and the billing/subscription lifecycle.
All Super Admin operations route through a dedicated DB engine connected
as ``m369_sa_runner`` (LOGIN, BYPASSRLS, NOSUPERUSER) — a separate
least-privilege role from the ordinary m369_app. The role's password is
provisioned via bootstrap SQL (\getenv M369_SA_RUNNER_PASSWORD), never
hardcoded, never shared with the migration service.

New endpoints (all under /api/v1/super-admin):
  - GET    /agencies                        list all (BYPASSRLS)
  - GET    /agencies/{id}                   detail with sub + member count
  - PATCH  /agencies/{id}                   name / is_active / brand_color
  - POST   /agencies/{id}/suspend           flip is_active=false (idempotent)
  - POST   /agencies/{id}/activate          re-activate (idempotent)
  - GET    /agencies/{id}/members           list memberships (cross-tenant)
  - PATCH  /agencies/{id}/members/{uid}     change role
  - GET/POST/PATCH /plans                   plan CRUD (Super Admin only)
  - GET/PATCH /subscriptions/{id}           lifecycle via state machine
  - GET    /payments                        list, filter by agency + status
  - POST   /payments/{id}/verify            idempotent manual verify
  - POST   /payments/{id}/reject            reject (terminal)
  - GET/PUT/DELETE /platform-settings/{key} upsert + delete
  - GET/POST/DELETE /agencies/{id}/notes    Super Admin notes on agencies
  - GET    /audit-logs                      SA-scoped audit log reader

Subscription lifecycle (services/billing.py):
  trial → active → past_due → suspended → cancelled
  Any → superseded (only via plan-change, not direct update)
  Disallowed transitions return 400.
  Price snapshot is frozen at creation — later plan price changes
  do NOT propagate to existing subscriptions.

Payment verification (services/billing.py):
  - Idempotent: re-verifying a verified payment is a no-op
  - Terminal states (rejected, expired) cannot be re-verified (409)
  - Cannot reject an already-verified payment (409)
  - txid is UNIQUE — duplicate inserts fail at DB level
  - amount_paid is INTEGER cents (never FLOAT)
  - Raw on-chain amount + decimals + exchange_rate stored separately
    for audit (e.g., 19.99 USDT TRC20 → amount_paid=1999,
    paid_amount_raw=19990000, paid_amount_decimals=6, exchange_rate=1.0)

Migrations:
  0008 — creates m369_sa_runner role (LOGIN + BYPASSRLS + NOSUPERUSER)
  0009 — widens payments.paid_currency from String(3) to String(10)
         so crypto codes like 'USDT' (4 chars) are accepted

Config + bootstrap:
  - DATABASE_URL_SUPER_ADMIN setting added with production guard
    (rejects 'm369_sa_runner_dev_password' in production)
  - docker-compose.yml: API service receives DATABASE_URL_SUPER_ADMIN,
    db service receives M369_SA_RUNNER_PASSWORD via \getenv
  - 01-bootstrap-roles.sql: provisions m369_sa_runner password via
    \getenv M369_SA_RUNNER_PASSWORD

Tests: 31 new tests in test_stage3_super_admin_billing.py:
  - Token separation (agency ↔ SA) in both directions
  - Agency CRUD + suspend/activate idempotency + audit
  - Member role changes
  - Plan CRUD + duplicate detection + seeded plan visibility
  - Subscription lifecycle + invalid transition 400 + price snapshot
  - Payment idempotent verify + terminal state rejection + txid UNIQUE
  - Financial precision: $19.99 stored as 1999 cents + raw on-chain
  - Platform settings + agency notes CRUD
  - Super Admin audit log queries
  - m369_sa_runner role attribute + table-privilege verification

Total: 128 tests passing (97 + 31). All run against real PostgreSQL 16.2
with real Alembic migrations 0001-0009.

Migration chain: 0001 → 0002 → 0003 → 0004 → 0005 → 0006 → 0007 → 0008 → 0009
Total tables: 23 (22 + alembic_version)
Total API endpoints: 67 (up from 41)
